#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362373 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c330648f-69ad-5778-98cb-bd48a0b160dd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Rate of Change of a Function in a Given Direction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd4a9e24-005a-5dfb-8480-4713eb0fefba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362375} {:answer/id #uuid "535f9046-a320-57a6-a8a3-35c141a42407" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362376} {:answer/id #uuid "269b3df3-6718-5e56-95a7-04bec75742f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{82}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362377} {:answer/id #uuid "da493b2b-9d48-57e0-82ee-bdf854cc43cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362378} {:answer/id #uuid "b6290e81-7555-5c3a-a4d9-f162c0d81c96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{80}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "269b3df3-6718-5e56-95a7-04bec75742f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{82}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362377} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f126513-a801-56d0-a2c4-55b140281628" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362374}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0d871812-574c-5223-8f52-1d1e692d14a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-36300" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)=2xy+{e}^{3x-y}.$ What is the rate of change of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(1,3)$ in the direction in which the function decreases most rapidly?" :question/worked-solution "At a given point, a function $f(x,y)$ decreases most rapidly in the opposite direction of its gradient at that point.\n\nIn our case, we compute $-∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(1,3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-∇\\,f(x,y) & =-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2xy+{e}^{3x-y})\\text{ }i-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy+{e}^{3x-y})\\text{ }j \\\\  & =-(2y+3{e}^{3x-y})\\text{ }i-(2x-{e}^{3x-y})\\text{ }j \\\\ -∇\\,f(1,3) & =-(2\\cdot 3+3\\cdot {e}^{3\\cdot 1-3})\\text{ }i-(2\\cdot 1-{e}^{3\\cdot 1-3})\\text{ }j \\\\  & =-9\\text{ }i-\\text{ }j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the rate of change of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(1,3)$ in the direction of $-∇f(1,3)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖-∇\\,f(1,3)‖ & =‖-9\\text{ }i-\\text{ }j‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-9)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{82}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
